# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers. A Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true would give them CRLF endings, and `sh` then fails with a
# `\r`-flavoured "not found" (exit 127) that is genuinely hard to read.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are consumed by the Linux build.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
